# scripts/public-hygiene.allow — exceptions for scripts/check-public-hygiene.sh, one per line:
#   item <I-number> <reason>     a placeholder item number the shipped text uses as an example
#   host <name> <reason>         a public DevStride host a stranger can visit
#   file <path> <reason>         a binary file (an image), which the check cannot read
# Every line carries its reason. Never loosen a pattern in the script to fit a hit: add a line
# here with a reason, or reword the text.

item I0000  the all-zero placeholder in examples
item I1234  a generic example item number
item I2000  an example item number in the planning skills
item I20100 the example plan root used throughout the loop's skills
item I20101 an example story under the example plan root
item I20102 an example story under the example plan root
item I20103 an example story under the example plan root
item I20104 an example story under the example plan root
item I20110 an example item in the build skills
item I20111 an example item in the build skills
item I20112 an example item in the build skills
item I20130 the example story in the build and review skills
item I20131 an example item in the build skills
item I20431 an example item in the release skills
item I201010 the prefix-collision example in the release-holds test (I20101 plus a digit)

host devstride.com       the public website, and the domain of public email addresses
host api.devstride.com   the public API and the hosted MCP endpoint
host app.devstride.com   the public web application
host docs.devstride.com  the public documentation site
